//*
# Answer questions from an MCP docs server

Needs an MCP configuration with a server named `docs` that exposes a `search` tool.
MCP tools are available only to agents; `restrict: { mcp }` limits which ones a block may call.

    spl run examples/mcp.spl --mcp mcp.json --arg "How do I configure authentication?"
*//

---
model: gpt-6-luna
---

const question = args[0] ?? 'How do I get started?';

---
mode: agent
restrict: { mcp: docs/search }

Use docs/search to answer @question
End with a line "Sources:" followed by the URLs of the pages you used ->[Str] @answer
---

assert(answer.includes('Sources:'), 'the answer does not cite its sources');

---
outputVar: summary
forbid: adding facts that are not in the answer

Rewrite this answer as at most five short bullet points followed by its sources: @answer
---

success(summary);
